    "q": "The sum of the digits of a two-digit number is 10. If the digits are reversed, the new number exceeds the original number by 36. What is the original number?",
    "opts": [
      "28",
      "46",
      "37",
      "73"
    ],
    "ans": 2,
    "sol": "Let tens digit be x and units digit be y. Original number N = 10x + y. Given x + y = 10. Reversed number = 10y + x. Difference: (10y + x) - (10x + y) = 9(y - x) = 36 => y - x = 4. Adding equations: 2y = 14 => y = 7. Thus x = 3. Original number = 10(3) + 7 = 37.",
    "form": "Reversal Difference = 9(y - x)",
    "exam": "GATE + Placement"
